{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdP2RhRuE3qvJKH8HgTYg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ABRJtnKeADH1cHryN2Aufm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/arena-ws.TkYsaz/SOLUTION.md","content":"# Solution\n\nTwo bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:\n\n1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** A cache hit returned the value without\n   calling `move_to_end(key)`, so reading an entry left it in its original\n   insertion position and it could be evicted as if it were least recently\n   used. Fixed by moving the key to the MRU end of the `OrderedDict` on every\n   valid (non-expired) hit.\n\n2. **`put` evicted on updates to existing keys.** The eviction check was\n   `len(self._data) >= self.capacity` with no regard for whether the key was\n   already present, so overwriting an existing key in a full cache wrongly\n   evicted the LRU entry (shrinking the cache below capacity). Fixed by only\n   evicting when the key is *not* already in the cache — an in-place update\n   never changes the entry count.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":191,"cache_read_input_tokens":25436,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":191,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"46f69fef-5bf6-4c7c-b5ab-c93c2e03fa71","uuid":"a205fdf3-d892-4b0e-90bc-e551c570eb6c","timestamp":"2026-07-25T15:38:23.766Z","request_id":"req_011CdP2RgjEUEA62dVa9Ksi6"}
